What is the sequence and numbering of the months in the Jewish calendar?
The sequence of the months in the Jewish calendar is as follows:

1. Nisan (usually corresponding to March-April in the Gregorian calendar)
2. Iyar
3. Sivan
4. Tammuz
5. Av
6. Elul
7. Tishrei (also known as September-October in the Gregorian calendar)
8. Cheshvan
9. Kislev
10. Tevet
11. Shevat
12. Adar (in non-leap years) or Adar II (in leap years)

Note that in leap years, an additional month called Adar II is added, which is a second Adar.
