What is the FM radio dial and how does it work?
The FM radio dial typically ranges from 87.5 to 108 MHz and is divided into several frequency bands. FM (Frequency Modulation) radio works by varying the frequency of the carrier wave in proportion to the amplitude of the audio signal. This variation in frequency is what allows the receiver to demodulate the signal and reproduce the original audio. The FM dial is usually divided into increments of 0.1 MHz (or 100 kHz), with each station occupying a specific frequency range.
