What was the Third Servile War and what was its historical context?
The Third Servile War was a slave rebellion against the Roman Republic, also known as the Gladiator War or the War of Spartacus. It was the last in a series of slave rebellions against the Roman Republic, known collectively as the Servile Wars. The war began in 73 BC, when around 70 slave-gladiators escaped from a gladiatorial school in Capua, led by the Thracian slave Spartacus. The rebellion was particularly alarming to Rome because its military seemed powerless to suppress it, and it directly threatened the Roman heartland of Italia.
