The statue was constructed during the 5th century BCE, a time of great cultural and artistic achievement in ancient Greece. It was built for the temple of Zeus at Olympia, a major sanctuary and site of the ancient Olympic Games. The statue was considered one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World and was renowned for its grandeur and artistic excellence.

